{"name":"Poisonous Potion","hex":"#99dd33","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"poisonous","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing sufficient poison to be dangerous to touch or ingest.","Of an animal such as a snake or spider, or parts of its body: producing a toxin intended for defensive or offensive use which is usually injected into an enemy or prey by biting or stinging; hence, of a bite or sting: injecting poison."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poisonous"},{"term":"potion","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small portion or dose of a liquid which is medicinal, poisonous, or magical."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To drug (someone)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/potion"}],"entries":[{"title":"Poison","blocks":[{"text":"In science, a poison is any chemical substance that is harmful or lethal to a living organism. The term of poison is used in a wide range of scientific fields and industries, where it is often specifically defined. It may also be applied colloquially or figuratively, with a broad sense."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/GHS-pictogram-skull.svg/330px-GHS-pictogram-skull.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poison","wikidata":"Q40867"},{"title":"Potion","blocks":[{"text":"A potion is a liquid that contains \"medicine, poison, or something that is supposed to have magic powers.\" It derives from the Latin word potio which refers to a drink or the act of drinking. The term philtre is also used, often specifically to describe a love potion, a potion that is believed to induce feelings of love or attraction in the one who drinks it.\nThroughout history, there have been several types of potions for a range of purposes. Reasons for taking potions have included curing an illness, securing immortality, and trying to inspire love. These potions, while often ineffective or poisonous, occasionally had some degree of medicinal benefits depending on what they sought to fix and the type and amount of ingredients used. Common ingredients in historical potions included Spanish fly, nightshade plants, cannabis, and opium."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Filtre_d%27Amour.jpg/330px-Filtre_d%27Amour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potion","wikidata":"Q1249918"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Saka-saka_-_cassava_leaves_in_mortar_and_pestle.jpg/500px-Saka-saka_-_cassava_leaves_in_mortar_and_pestle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Saka-saka_-_cassava_leaves_in_mortar_and_pestle.jpg/500px-Saka-saka_-_cassava_leaves_in_mortar_and_pestle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cassava leaves contain cyanide and can thus cause poisoning if not prepared correctly.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaka-saka_-_cassava_leaves_in_mortar_and_pestle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Lagoa_vermelha_na_Mina_do_Losal_05.jpg/500px-Lagoa_vermelha_na_Mina_do_Losal_05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Lagoa_vermelha_na_Mina_do_Losal_05.jpg/500px-Lagoa_vermelha_na_Mina_do_Losal_05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Polluted groundwater, in this case depicting acid mine drainage, can cause chronic poisoning.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALagoa_vermelha_na_Mina_do_Losal_05.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Jan_Matejko-Poisoning_of_Queen_Bona.jpg/500px-Jan_Matejko-Poisoning_of_Que